1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:01,910
It's six forty-five

2
00:00:01,920 --> 00:00:03,380
in the morning.

3
00:00:03,390 --> 00:00:05,990
Marco just called in sick.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,640
Four customers are waiting

5
00:00:07,650 --> 00:00:09,120
for him today.

6
00:00:09,130 --> 00:00:11,660
Who covers his jobs?

7
00:00:11,670 --> 00:00:12,750
Figuring that out

8
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:15,120
by hand takes an hour.

9
00:00:15,130 --> 00:00:16,630
Second Shift does it

10
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:17,850
in seconds.

11
00:00:18,190 --> 00:00:20,970
Someone posts in Slack:

12
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:22,690
Marco is out.

13
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:24,510
Second Shift reads it,

14
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:26,250
then looks at every job

15
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:28,060
and every calendar.

16
00:00:28,390 --> 00:00:30,580
It builds a new plan.

17
00:00:30,590 --> 00:00:32,770
Watch the trucks move.

18
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:34,670
Wei can do Marco's

19
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:36,310
big gas job,

20
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:38,010
but he's busy.

21
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:39,300
So Ana takes

22
00:00:39,310 --> 00:00:41,060
Wei's small job,

23
00:00:41,070 --> 00:00:43,400
and Wei takes Marco's.

24
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:44,820
One job can't

25
00:00:44,830 --> 00:00:46,610
be saved today,

26
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:48,210
so that customer is asked

27
00:00:48,220 --> 00:00:50,010
to pick a new time.

28
00:00:50,390 --> 00:00:52,130
Nothing changes until

29
00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:54,270
a person says yes.

30
00:00:54,280 --> 00:00:55,500
One click,

31
00:00:55,510 --> 00:00:57,360
and it updates the calendars

32
00:00:57,370 --> 00:00:58,890
and the job sheet,

33
00:00:58,900 --> 00:01:01,310
messages the team in Slack,

34
00:01:01,320 --> 00:01:03,320
and emails the customers.

35
00:01:03,458 --> 00:01:06,568
Then it double-checks every change.

36
00:01:06,578 --> 00:01:09,948
Thirty-six out of thirty-six.

37
00:01:09,958 --> 00:01:12,408
If it crashes halfway,

38
00:01:12,418 --> 00:01:13,478
it finishes

39
00:01:13,488 --> 00:01:16,578
without sending anything twice.

40
00:01:16,588 --> 00:01:18,308
And you can ask:

41
00:01:18,318 --> 00:01:19,258
what if Wei

42
00:01:19,268 --> 00:01:20,768
doesn't show up?

43
00:01:20,778 --> 00:01:22,228
It shows you,

44
00:01:22,238 --> 00:01:23,970
before it happens.

45
00:01:24,138 --> 00:01:25,338
Sick days,

46
00:01:25,348 --> 00:01:28,388
flat tires, no-shows.

47
00:01:28,398 --> 00:01:30,588
They'll keep happening.

48
00:01:30,598 --> 00:01:32,508
Now they take seconds

49
00:01:32,518 --> 00:01:33,967
to fix,

50
00:01:33,978 --> 00:01:35,678
not an hour.

51
00:01:35,688 --> 00:01:38,157
We can't predict the day.

52
00:01:38,168 --> 00:01:39,808
But we can be ready

53
00:01:39,818 --> 00:01:40,888
for it.

54
00:01:40,898 --> 00:01:42,208
Second Shift.

